---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../styles/global.css';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/') ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
---
<Layout title="Glorious Chariot" active="Hangar">
  <section class="detail-hero"><div class="page-wrap detail-grid"><div class="detail-copy"><p class="kicker">Hangar file 01 // ownership disputed</p><h1>Glorious<br />Chariot</h1><p class="lede">A luxury 3000-class space yacht built by SoroSuub, then customised for Darga the Hutt, then liberated by people who had run out of patience.</p><div class="stamp">GLORIOUS CHARIOT<br />STATUS: OPERATIONAL / PRIVATEER<br />CREW: 1 + PASSENGERS: 10<br />CURRENT OWNER: THE CREW, APPARENTLY</div></div><img class="detail-image" src={`${base}images/glorious-chariot.png`} alt="The Glorious Chariot on its reinforced landing bay" /></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="page-wrap detail-grid"><div><p class="kicker">Manifest</p><h2>Built for decadence.<br />Refitted for survival.</h2><p class="lede" style="margin-top:24px">Darga’s original interior was once very nice. Then it became a den of iniquity, a storage problem, and eventually our problem. We kept the useful bits, stripped the disgusting bits, and added enough armour to make the ship look intentional.</p><div class="spec-table"><div class="spec-row"><span>Class</span><strong>Luxury 3000 space yacht</strong></div><div class="spec-row"><span>Capacity</span><strong>1 crew / 10 passengers</strong></div><div class="spec-row"><span>Cargo</span><strong>100 tons, plus whatever Maurice insists is essential</strong></div><div class="spec-row"><span>Hyperdrive</span><strong>Class 2 / backup class 14</strong></div><div class="spec-row"><span>Defence</span><strong>Shields, armour, flush hardpoints, plausible deniability</strong></div><div class="spec-row"><span>Acquisition</span><strong>Darga died. We took the keys.</strong></div></div></div><div class="plate about-card"><p class="kicker">Crew assessment</p><h3>“It has a cargo hatch now.”</h3><p style="margin-top:20px">The Chariot is our showpiece, our refuge, and our most visible admission that subtlety has failed. It holds ten passengers in comfort, carries enough kit to make an Imperial quartermaster nervous, and lands on a pad that is finally proportionate to its ego.</p><p>Do not ask what happened to the previous owner. The answer is in the travelogue.</p></div></div></section>
</Layout>
